{"description":"`go test ./...` in eka-cli does not complete: it panics at the 5-minute timeout in a different test each run (TestRetireCascadeCmt, TestRetireAsArchived, TestSyncAdoptRefusalsExitTwo, TestGetNumberField, TestNewContentFile observed across runs), always parked in modernc.org/sqlite Store.Close -\u003e _walCheckpoint -\u003e Xfsync. Reproduced on a pristine `git archive HEAD` tree under /tmp/base, so it predates the working tree. Unaffected by -test.parallel 1, TMPDIR=/dev/shm and timeouts from 60s to 600s.","impact":"The command that verifies a release cannot be run in this environment, so releases rely on partitioned runs of the cmd package plus per-package runs — a workaround that is easy to skip and that no script enforces. verify-release.sh covers version axes, not tests.","acceptanceCriteria":"- Root cause named: the WAL checkpoint fsync path on this filesystem, a missing connection pragma, or a leaked open handle keeping a store busy.\n- `go test ./... -count=1` completes green twice in a row on a tree with no test change.\n- If the cause is environmental, the failure is detected and named in the test setup (skip with a reason) instead of surfacing as a random timeout."}